Problem: the Windows backend PR job failed twice in the real MCP stdio integration test because Beaver clears child-process environments and omitted SystemRoot. Node 24 on Windows then aborts during startup when its CSPRNG initialization cannot access the Windows system configuration; the parent observes only a closed stdin pipe. Root-cause evidence: the isolated test passed 12/12 with Node 22, failed immediately with Node 24, and a direct environment matrix showed Node 24 exit code 134 without SystemRoot but stayed alive with SystemRoot. Objective: keep MCP child environments restricted while restoring Node 24 and Windows compatibility. Decision: add only SystemRoot on Windows, canonicalize it, require an absolute existing root containing System32, and fail closed with a generic error if absent or invalid. Unix code paths are unchanged. Tests: added Windows coverage for preservation and rejection of missing/relative roots; Node 24 MCP round trip passed 12/12 before final cleanup and 3/3 after; cargo test --lib --features windows-tests -- --test-threads=1 passed 2972, failed 0, ignored 4; cargo clippy --lib --features windows-tests -- -A dead-code -D warnings passed; cargo fmt --check and git diff --check passed; graphify update . completed.
